<!--
  gradlew checkSetup checkEntrypoint checkRestore checkPipeSafety

  All four shell suites in one run: the installer's checks, the Minecraft entrypoint, the restore
  guards and the pipefail scan. The scripts they test run on the Linux host and in the containers.

  NONE OF THEM NEEDS DOCKER OR A NETWORK - that is the point of them. They drive the scripts'
  functions directly, which is why they can hang off `check` at all.

  They shell out to `bash` off PATH and need bash 4 or later. Where there is none, as on Windows,
  each one says so and is skipped rather than failed; CI always runs them.
-->
